    "12",
    "1 whole turkey"
  ],
  "categories": [
    "Dinner"
  ],
  "cuisines": [
    "American"
  ],
  "regions": [
    "American"
  ],
  "breadcrumbs": [],
  "keywords": [],
  "ingredients": [
    "0.5 cup cold butter",
    "1 (12 pound) whole turkey, neck and giblets removed",
    "1 tablespoon vegetable oil",
    "2 Granny Smith apples - cored, peeled, and cut into 8 wedges each",
    "1 large onion, cut into 8 wedges",
    "0.5 whole head garlic, separated into cloves and peeled",
    "1 pound celery, cut into 2-inch lengths",
    "1 tablespoon poultry seasoning"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients. Preheat oven to 325 degrees F (165 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/AMhjZ8NzYqBi7nj493gE-a2F7mg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-230121-very-moist-and-flavorful-roast-turkey-VAT-step-01-c3e6fa02513f4f86adf1941ff8c5614f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/230121/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cut butter into 1-tablespoon pieces, quarter the pieces, and refrigerate butter until needed.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/iiVhqCdY9p3jfi6pBZnyKmaYbeU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-230121-very-moist-and-flavorful-roast-turkey-VAT-step-02-1-e9df67ddbecb4630a050dd29535c5fae.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/230121/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use your fingers to loosen the skin over the turkey breast and thighs. Cut a hole in the turkey skin between tail and body (to affix legs); cut a hole on each side of the turkey beneath each wing (to affix wings). Rub the entire skin with vegetable oil.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/sdH_FYxA6SsyI2YZUb7pQqQ9EOw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-230121-very-moist-and-flavorful-roast-turkey-VAT-step-03-2rubbingoil-1a1d12531a88461ba7b2712c48b07613.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/230121/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toss apple and onion wedges, garlic cloves, and celery in a large bowl until combined; sprinkle poultry seasoning over the apple mixture and toss again to coat.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Cg4C1HKOIKkuOPGvODnOoIHVNX8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-230121-very-moist-and-flavorful-roast-turkey-VAT-step-04-8c62220035824ce1ad497787220c5141.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/230121/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stuff the body and neck cavities with the apple mixture. Insert each wing tip into the hole under the wing to secure wings; insert both legs into hole near tail to secure legs.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/ylilH90pVNjecYXXmRcdzytEpg0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-230121-very-moist-and-flavorful-roast-turkey-VAT-step-05-9ce1c7c8030a4bd59e7275cc973a8233.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/230121/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place turkey onto a rack and set in a roasting pan. Insert cold butter pieces under the loosened skin, distributing the butter as evenly as possible.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/EMbw8lPVaKpllYec_l2ZWBoFqEY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-230121-very-moist-and-flavorful-roast-turkey-VAT-step-06-1handinframe-6700feb6ccdf49a2872a13823ca7b276.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/230121/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast the turkey in the preheated oven until an instant-read meat thermometer inserted into the thickest part of a thigh, not touching bone, reads 160 degrees F (70 degrees C), about 3 1/2 hours. Check for doneness after 3 hours.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/MadEDPALWJQbcCjHWYIHsdM1TS4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-230121-very-moist-and-flavorful-roast-turkey-VAT-step-07-f1d7fdad4150473aab72f92ec3fd6263.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/230121/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove roasting pan containing turkey from oven and cover with aluminum foil, lightly pressing the foil directly onto the bird. Let the turkey rest for 40 minutes before carving.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/pktEOVqCv5dqQgt4NXa6kztozCs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-230121-very-moist-and-flavorful-roast-turkey-VAT-step-08-1-0f47f62517b04400b29adee798f4038b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/230121/step_08.webp"
    }
  ],
